## 2026-02-04 (UTC)

### Goal
Wire the backend to expose Library items from the existing Postgres tables so the frontend `Library` tab can query real data.

### Implementation (Library APIs)
- Added SQLModel models/schemas for `library_item` in:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/models.py`
- Added Library router:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/routes/library.py`
- Registered router:
  - `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/api/main.py`

### Endpoints (current)
- `GET /api/v1/library/` (authenticated)
  - filters: `workflow_key`, `kind`, `q`, `current_only`, `skip`, `limit`
- `GET /api/v1/library/workflow-keys` (authenticated)
  - returns distinct `workflow_key` values (buckets) with counts
- `GET /api/v1/library/{id}` (authenticated)
- `POST /api/v1/library/` (superuser)
- `PUT /api/v1/library/{id}` (superuser)
  - **supersede semantics**: creates a new row and sets `superseded_by_id` on the previous row (never mutates content in-place)
